fr:mainmatter.html:p:
A displayed category \overline {\mathcal {D}} over a base category \mathcal {C} packages the data of a category that "lies over" \mathcal {C}: each object and each morphism of \mathcal {C} is equipped with a fiber of objects and morphisms displayed atop it. It consists of
For each object x : \mathcal {c}_{0}, a type of displayed objects \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x} lying over x. We write \overline {x} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x} for a displayed object over x.
For each morphism f : \mathcal {C} {\mathopen {}\left (x , y\right )\mathclose {}} and displayed objects \overline {x} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x} and \overline {y} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{y}, a set of displayed morphisms \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}} lying over f. We write such a displayed morphism \overline {g} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}} as \overline {g} : \overline {x} \to _{f} \overline {y} or \overline {x} \overset {\overline {g}}{\to _{f}} \overline {y}, subscripting the arrow with the base morphism f it lies over.
A displayed composition operation. For f : x \to y and g : y \to z with displayed morphisms \overline {f} : \overline {x} \to _{f} \overline {y} and \overline {g} : \overline {y} \to _{g} \overline {z}, there is a displayed morphism \overline {f} \star \overline {g} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f \star g}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {z}\right )\mathclose {}} lying over the composite f \star g.
For each \overline {x} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x}, a displayed identity \mathsf {id}_{\overline {x}} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{\mathsf {id}_{x}}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {x}\right )\mathclose {}} lying over \mathsf {id}_{x}.
Left-unitality, displayed: for all \overline {f} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}}, a heterogeneous equality \overline {\mathsf {idL}_{f}} : \mathsf {id}_{\overline {x}} \star \overline {f} =_{\mathsf {idL}_{f}} \overline {f}
Right-unitality, displayed: for all \overline {f} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}}, a heterogeneous equality \overline {\mathsf {idR}_{f}} : \overline {f} \star \mathsf {id}_{\overline {y}} =_{\mathsf {idR}_{f}} \overline {f}
Associativity, displayed: for all \overline {f}, \overline {g}, \overline {h} over f : x \to y, g : y \to z, h : z \to w, a heterogeneous equality \overline {\mathsf {assoc}_{f , g , h}} : {\mathopen {}\left (\overline {f} \star {\mathopen {}\left (\overline {g} \star \overline {h}\right )\mathclose {}}\right )\mathclose {}} =_{\mathsf {assoc}_{f , g , h}} {\mathopen {}\left ({\mathopen {}\left (\overline {f} \star \overline {g}\right )\mathclose {}} \star \overline {h}\right )\mathclose {}}

